# OPDP import rules

The rules of importing the whole OPDP atlas, kept apart from the reading and the
writing so each is a fact anyone can check. The release is one line of JSON; the
importer starts a new line before every `{"problem_id":` (a quote that is not
escaped never occurs inside a JSON string, so the break always falls between
tokens) and then reads the lines back into records, joining any line a nested
object split until the text parses.

## Note
A record's cohort, from the dataset version that added it to the atlas.

## To cohortKeyOf (version: Text) -> Text:
    Let versions be ["1.2.0", "1.5.0", "1.6.0", "1.7.0", "1.8.0"].
    Let keys be ["unsolvedmath", "aim", "oberwolfach", "mathdb", "proofatlas"].
    Let mutable i be 0.
    Repeat for v in versions:
        Set i to i + 1.
        If v is equal to version:
            Return item i of keys.
    Return "opdp-" + version.

## Note
Whether a line ends the header (the release's notes hold record-shaped objects
too, so records are only read after the line that opens the records array),
whether a line begins a record, and the record text a buffer of lines holds once
its separator is dropped: the comma before the next record, or the bracket and
brace that close the array and the document after the last.

## To opensRecords (line: Text) -> Bool:
    Return endsWith(trimEnd(line), "\"records\":[").

## To isRecordStart (line: Text) -> Bool:
    Return startsWith(line, "{{\"problem_id\":").

## To recordCandidate (buffer: Text) -> Text:
    Let t be trimEnd(buffer).
    If endsWith(t, "]}}"):
        Return removeSuffix(t, "]}}").
    Return removeSuffix(t, ",").

## Note
A MathDB record holds a public-list excerpt, not a statement; it must be
completed from its cited source before it can be formalized, and MathDB's terms
cap detail fetches, so it is never fetched in bulk. Its unit waits behind full
statements at a quarter of its rank, and its worker is told why.

## To isExcerptOnly (textMode: Text) -> Bool:
    Return textMode is equal to "mathdb_public_list_excerpt".

## To excerptDivisor () -> Int:
    Return 4.

## To unitPriority (rank: Int, excerpt: Bool) -> Int:
    If excerpt:
        Return rank / excerptDivisor().
    Return rank.

## To excerptContext () -> Text:
    Return "This statement is a MathDB public-list excerpt, not a complete problem. Complete it from its cited source first; never fetch MathDB pages in bulk.".

## Test: opdp import names each dataset version a cohort

Expect that cohortKeyOf("1.2.0") is equal to "unsolvedmath".
Expect that cohortKeyOf("1.7.0") is equal to "mathdb".
Expect that cohortKeyOf("1.8.0") is equal to "proofatlas".
Expect that cohortKeyOf("2.0.0") is equal to "opdp-2.0.0".

## Test: opdp import reads records back from their lines

Expect that isRecordStart("{{\"problem_id\":7,\"title\":\"x\"}},") is equal to true.
Expect that isRecordStart("{{\"format_name\":\"x\"") is equal to false.
Expect that opensRecords("{{\"problem_id\":\"Stable id\"}}]}},\"records\":[") is equal to true.
Expect that opensRecords("{{\"problem_id\":7}},") is equal to false.
Expect that recordCandidate("{{\"problem_id\":7}},") is equal to "{{\"problem_id\":7}}".
Expect that recordCandidate("{{\"problem_id\":7}}]}}") is equal to "{{\"problem_id\":7}}".
Expect that jsonValid(recordCandidate("{{\"problem_id\":7,\"a\":[1]}}]}}\n")) is equal to true.

## Test: opdp import puts excerpts behind full statements

For all booleans excerpt:
    Let p be unitPriority(8000, excerpt).
    Expect that p is at most 8000.
    Expect that (p is equal to 8000) is equal to (excerpt is equal to false).
    Expect that isExcerptOnly("mathdb_public_list_excerpt") is equal to true.
